THIRD-PARTY MODELS AND DATA

The MIT licence above covers this repository's own code. It does not relicense
the model weights or the datasets, which carry their own terms.

A small set of sample inputs from three of these datasets IS included, under
samples/ — two cases per modality, so the upload paths can be exercised without
fetching a dataset first. No training or validation split is included, and no
patient data is. samples/README.md names each dataset, its size and its
attribution requirement.

  - MedGemma (google/medgemma-*) — Google Health AI Developer Foundations
    terms of use. Not distributed with this repository; download it yourself
    and accept the terms at that point.

  - CAMUS — the echocardiography segmentation dataset, released for research
    use by the University of Lyon (CREATIS). Cite the dataset paper if you
    publish results derived from the echo checkpoint. Two patients are included
    under samples/echo/, each shipping the dataset's own required citation
    file; the frames are gzipped but otherwise unmodified.

  - MedHK23/CCA — the coronary CT angiography dataset behind the CCTA
    checkpoint, 20 volumes. Two of them are included under samples/ccta/ with
    their ground truth; the other 18 are not. Check the dataset's terms at the
    source before redistributing anything derived from it.

  - PTB-XL — the 12-lead ECG dataset, published on PhysioNet under the Open
    Data Commons Attribution Licence v1.0. Attribution is required. Two records
    are included under samples/ecg/.

  - segmentation-models-pytorch, timm, PyTorch and the other dependencies —
    their own licences, unchanged, as resolved by your package manager.
